From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Dalessio <mike.dalessio@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 10 Jun 2026 15:52:50 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] fix(CRuby): out-of-bounds read in NodeSet#[] with large
 negative index

index_at checked the offset with abs((int)offset), truncating the
64-bit index to 32 bits. A large negative index could pass the check
but then be used at full width to read outside the node table. Compare
the full-width offset against the bounds instead.

ref: https://github.com/sparklemotion/nokogiri/security/advisories/GHSA-5prr-v3j2-97mh

Fixes: CVE-2026-57235

[Shivani: backported to nokogiri-1.13.6; dropped the JRuby-only
XmlNodeSet.java hunk and test changes since this package ships only
the CRuby C extension]
Signed-off-by: Shivani Agarwal <shivani.agarwal@broadcom.com>
---
 ext/nokogiri/xml_node_set.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/ext/nokogiri/xml_node_set.c b/ext/nokogiri/xml_node_set.c
index 5670371..006fb41 100644
--- a/ext/nokogiri/xml_node_set.c
+++ b/ext/nokogiri/xml_node_set.c
@@ -297,7 +297,7 @@ index_at(VALUE self, long offset)
 
   Data_Get_Struct(self, xmlNodeSet, node_set);
 
-  if (offset >= node_set->nodeNr || abs((int)offset) > node_set->nodeNr) {
+  if (offset >= node_set->nodeNr || offset < -node_set->nodeNr) {
     return Qnil;
   }
 
